<Base title="Privacy" description="What TheTravelFact does with a visit. No accounts; Google cookies for analytics and ads.">
  <article class="shell page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Updated 22 November 2026.</p>
    <p>TheTravelFact does not run accounts, comments, or a contact form. If you email contact@thetravelfact.com, we read that mail to answer it or to correct a page. Do not send sensitive documents.</p>
    <p>The site uses Google Analytics to count visits, and Google AdSense to show ads. Google and its partners may use cookies to serve ads based on your visits to this and other websites, and to measure visits here. You can opt out of personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google's Ads Settings</a>. Third-party vendors and ad networks may also place and read cookies, or use web beacons, in connection with the ads shown here.</p>
    <p>The Amazon adapter link leaves this site. Amazon can set its own cookies under its own policy, and the link includes the associate tag thetravelfact-20. Hotel and tour slots are not links yet, so they do not hand you to those companies.</p>
    <p>The site is built to be hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes the request that delivers the page. Their role is described in Cloudflare's own privacy notice.</p>
    <p>Questions about this policy go to the same address, contact@thetravelfact.com.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
